tool_objectfs hands \Aws\S3\S3Client::factory() only region, credentials and
endpoint. The AWS SDK bundled with Moodle 4.5 defaults use_path_style_endpoint
to false, and its S3 endpoint ruleset then rewrites a custom http endpoint to
{scheme}://{Bucket}.{authority}{path}. SeaweedFS serves path-style only and the
internal endpoint is a bare service name, so the virtual-host host never
resolves. The plugin exposes no setting for this, so the client option is
forced here.

Generated with `diff -u` against the pinned commit and applied with `-F0`, so
the build fails instead of letting GNU patch's default fuzz factor discard
context and land the hunk somewhere upstream moved it to.

--- a/classes/local/store/s3/client.php
+++ b/classes/local/store/s3/client.php
@@ -182,6 +182,7 @@
         // Support base_url config for aws api compatible endpoints.
         if ($config->s3_base_url) {
             $options['endpoint'] = $config->s3_base_url;
+            $options['use_path_style_endpoint'] = true;
         }

         $this->client = \Aws\S3\S3Client::factory($options);
